From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:49:54 +0300
Subject: context: ppc64 sysv elf: keep F14-F31, FPSCR and V20-V31
 across a switch

jump_fcontext and ontop_fcontext for ppc64 (ELFv1 and ELFv2) saved only the
non-volatile general registers, CR and (since late 2024) V31. The ABI also has
F14-F31 non-volatile (and V20-V31 with AltiVec), and FPSCR is a limited-access
register a call must not change. A double that the compiler keeps in F14 across
fiber::resume() came back with the other context's value: a test that keeps
twelve doubles live across resume() in both contexts failed on ppc64 (qemu,
Debian sid, 1.92.0), as did the same with AltiVec vectors at -maltivec.

The context data grows from 200 to 552 bytes: F14-F31 at 200, FPSCR at 344,
V20-V31 at 360 (16-byte aligned, as the frame size is 8 mod 16 like before);
the V31 save at 184 goes into that block, so 184 is the back-chain again.
make_fcontext reserves 552 + 48 bytes and gives the new context the creator's
FPSCR. The ppc32 code saves F14-F31 and FPSCR the same way.

diff --git a/libs/context/src/asm/jump_ppc64_sysv_elf_gas.S b/libs/context/src/asm/jump_ppc64_sysv_elf_gas.S
--- a/libs/context/src/asm/jump_ppc64_sysv_elf_gas.S
+++ b/libs/context/src/asm/jump_ppc64_sysv_elf_gas.S
@@ -66,6 +66,17 @@
  *                                                     *
  *******************************************************/
 
+/*******************************************************
+ *  Below the 200 bytes above (offsets from the context *
+ *  pointer, total 552 bytes, a multiple of 16 plus 8   *
+ *  so that offset 360 is 16-byte aligned):             *
+ *  200-343  F14-F31                                    *
+ *  344      FPSCR                                      *
+ *  352      (padding)                                  *
+ *  360-551  V20-V31, 16 bytes each                     *
+ *  The slot at 184 is the back-chain only.             *
+ *******************************************************/
+
 .file "jump_ppc64_sysv_elf_gas.S"
 .globl jump_fcontext
 .hidden jump_fcontext
@@ -98,7 +109,7 @@ jump_fcontext:
 # endif
 #endif
     # reserve space on stack
-    subi  %r1, %r1, 200
+    subi  %r1, %r1, 552
 
 #if _CALL_ELF != 2
     std  %r2,  0(%r1)  # save TOC
@@ -134,8 +145,51 @@ jump_fcontext:
     # save LR as PC
     std   %r0, 176(%r1)
 
-    # Save VS63
-    li    %r31, 184
+    # save F14-F31 and FPSCR (callee-saved / limited-access in the ABI)
+    stfd  %f14, 200(%r1)
